posts.body:
Add your custom keys to the Input.keyMapper (or get a plugin for custom keys).
I always like to access everything by using the "forceSelect" and "processOk". If your commands are fixed (like 0 attack, 1 skills, 2 guard, 3 items), I think you can just do something like below to check the keyboard presses in processHandling (like the base keys). If the commands vary, you'll need additional code to get the correct index. (I only wrote two keys there, continue the list.)
const _MyEdit1_actorCommand_processHandling = Window_ActorCommand.prototype.processHandling;
Window_ActorCommand.prototype.processHandling = function() {
if (this.isOpenAndActive()) {
if (Input.isTriggered("a")) {
this.forceSelect(0);
return this.processOk();
}
if (Input.isTriggered("s")) {
this.forceSelect(1);
return this.processOk();
}
}
_MyEdit1_actorCommand_processHandling.call(this);
}
EDIT:
Might add the
if (this.isOpenAndActive())
at the beginning of your custom check list too (just to be sure?)
EDIT2: Added the above conditional into the code and also added the return statements in the triggers.

